// `SelfBuff` always inserts its buff on the caster only
// (common/src/states/self_buff.rs: `entity: data.entity`) -- it has no
// reach onto other entities at all, so the sheet's own "deafens [nearby
// creatures], hinders their approach, disperses gas/fog" riders are dropped
// entirely: no target-other-entities primitive exists on this variant to
// hook them into (contrast BasicAura, which does reach nearby allies, but
// isn't the variant assigned here). What survives is the purely
// self-protective half of the flavor ("buffets anyone who tries to draw
// near") modeled with the existing `ProtectingWard` BuffKind (flat damage
// reduction) as the closest defensive analogue to a swirling wind shell
// around the caster -- the same "closest existing BuffKind, not a new one"
// discipline this whole batch follows. Genuinely sustained for the full
// 60 s via `BuffData.duration`, so unlike flame_blade.ron/
// spiritual_weapon.ron in this same batch, the Concentration(60) framing is
// real here and is kept as-is.
SelfBuff(
    buildup_duration: 0.4,
    cast_duration: 0.3,
    recover_duration: 0.3,
    buffs: [
        BuffDesc(kind: ProtectingWard, data: BuffData(strength: 0.3, duration: Some(60.0))),
    ],
    energy_cost: 45,
    meta: (school: Some(Evocation), source: Some(Arcane)),
)
